WHY THIS IS NOT AN MIT LICENCE. This repository holds compiled installers, not
source code, and HuddleOwl is not open source. Putting an MIT licence here would
say the application may be copied, modified and redistributed by anyone, which
is not true and would contradict the licence key the paid tier is sold under.
What follows is what you may actually do.

The third-party components bundled inside the installers keep their own
licences, which are permissive and are reproduced in full in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md in this repository. Nothing here changes those terms, and
nothing in those terms changes these.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   Download, install and use HuddleOwl on machines you control. Use it for work,
   including commercial work. Run it for as long as you like.

   Individual use of the on-device features is free, with no account and no
   payment. The cloud engines require a paid licence key.

   Recommend it, write about it, link to it, and link people to this repository
   to download it.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Redistribute, resell or rehost the installers, or charge anyone for access to
   them. Point people at this repository instead, so they get a build that has
   not been modified.

   Rebrand the application or present it as your own product.

   Remove or alter the third-party notices that ship with it.

   Reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the application, except where that
   right cannot be excluded by law that applies to you.

   Share a licence key with anyone outside the seat it was bought for.

   To deploy HuddleOwl across an organisation, ask. That is a conversation
   rather than a refusal: hello@huddleowl.com.

3. NO WARRANTY

   HuddleOwl is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability,
   fitness for a particular purpose and noninfringement.

   Coaching cues and scores are a model's opinion about a conversation, and they
   are wrong sometimes. Do not treat the output as a system of record, a legal
   record, or a performance assessment of anybody.

4. RECORDING IS YOUR RESPONSIBILITY

   HuddleOwl records audio on your machine at your instruction. Consent and
   recording law vary by country, and by state or province within several of
   them. Following the law where you and the other participants are is yours to
   do, not ours.

5. LIABILITY

   In no event shall the author be liable for any claim, damages or other
   liability, whether in an action of contract, tort or otherwise, arising from,
   out of or in connection with the software or its use.

The current version of these terms is published at https://huddleowl.com/terms.
